{
  "id": "pump-house-nine",
  "name": "Pump House Nine",
  "description": "The main floor of Pump House Nine on the edge of Drownworks' Fourth Settling Bay, where Ines's night crew keeps the mains under half the Ribbon steady. Two big old cast-iron pumps in faded teal-green stand on concrete plinths, valve wheels and pressure dials on their casings, thick pipes rising into the ceiling. Behind them a wall of tall steel-framed windows looks out on the settling bay glowing teal at night, catwalks across it, filtration halls and the city's towers beyond. On the left, steel steps up to a control desk with switches, indicator lamps, a green CRT flow graph, a wall phone, a cork board and an amber warning beacon. On the right, the crew corner: lockers, a bench, an oilcloth coat on a hook, a kettle and mugs, a first-aid cabinet, and a heavy door to the stairs. Caged lamps hang from the crane rail overhead.",
